# .gitignore — every exclusion carries its rationale.
# If you add a line here, say why. An unexplained exclusion becomes an
# unexplained missing file six months later. (kb/git-discipline.md)

# --- Secrets and PII ---------------------------------------------------------
# Logins, portal credentials, API keys. NEVER commit these.
# If one is ever committed it is burned — rotate it, don't just delete the line.
.env
.env.local
**/credentials.json

# Identity documents, account numbers, screening reports. These stay OUT of
# version control entirely; tracked prose refers to them by path only.
**/_private/

# --- Machine-local Claude Code state -----------------------------------------
# Per-machine permission grants. The REST of .claude/ (commands, settings.json)
# IS tracked: it holds the project's permission policy and slash commands.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Regenerable / scratch ---------------------------------------------------
# Working/ holds interrupted-run scratchpads. A scratch file that matters gets
# routed to kb/ or a real folder by `close the session`; the rest is transient.
Working/

# Microsoft Office temp lock files
~$*

# Python bytecode and the venv (rebuilt from kb/platform-and-tools.md).
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY TRACKED (do not add these):
#   Inbox/     — drops awaiting triage plus the _Manifest.md decision ledger.
#   Archive/   — safety-net backups and processed originals. Provenance.
#   Outbox/    — what the owner reads, opened from the repo.
#   .kit.json  — which files came from the Starter Kit, for scripts/kit_sync.py.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Desk and lane ------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local stall telemetry written by the PermissionRequest hook
# (scripts/note_prompt.py). The rest of coordination/ — the desk record, the
# launch record, task sheets, the desk log, closed/ archives — IS tracked: it
# is the job's provenance, and desk_save.py commits it with the job.
coordination/prompts.jsonl
coordination/prompts.jsonl.1
